text:
mariam: Heads up — customer reported console shows 2x token charge for a single streaming request that retried and then made a tool call which got truncated. Console trace shows final model tokens only, ledger shows provisional + confirmed. :confused;
kevin: do we have the session id or logs?;
mariam: session=usr-73f2, router route=eu-west-1-a, attempt=1 -> stream starts, partial tokens 420 provisional. then client reconnect, attempt=2 -> resumed prefix 420 + toolcall truncated -> final confirmed 560. Ledger rows:

# ledger events
ts=1768004318 session=usr-73f2 attempt=1 event=provisional_charge tokens=420 route_tag=eu-west-1-a provisional=true
ts=1768004324 session=usr-73f2 attempt=2 event=confirmed_charge tokens=560 route_tag=eu-west-1-b provisional=false
ts=1768004324 session=usr-73f2 attempt=2 event=toolcall_truncate tokens=80 route_tag=eu-west-1-b provisional=false

mariam: console UI shows `560 tokens` but customer invoice line items sum 420+560=980 which is wrong.;
jess: are we double-counting because provisional events are still in final ledger export? we should mark provisional as reversed/zeroed on confirm.;
kevin: currently provisional events are written as independent rows and downstream billing export dedupes only when session+attempt match. since attempt changed on reconnect we lost the link.;
oliver: what about adding an idempotency key at router level that survives reconnects (session-level billing id)? then confirmed would reference that billing_id and we can mark provisional events as superseded.;
mariam: +1. minimal change might be to include `billing_session_id` in every ledger row and include `supersedes=<billing_id>` on confirmed rows. then export can drop provisional when superseded.;
jess: also need console UX to differentiate provisional vs confirmed and show why provisional wasn't collapsed — e.g., route changed or attempt bump. propose tooltip: "provisional charge not auto-credited because route_tag changed: eu-west-1-a -> eu-west-1-b".;
kevin: agree. also we should log `router_route` and `attempt_id` in metric labels for token telemetry so dashboards can correlate. dashboards currently slice by model & route_tag only, missing attempt and billing_session_id.;
mariam: implementation proposal:
- runtime: attach billing_session_id to incoming request; if reconnect occurs within Xs try to reuse billing_session_id unless customer explicitly resets.
- ledger: add fields billing_session_id, attempt_id, provisional(boolean), supersedes(optional).
- export: dedupe on billing_session_id, prefer confirmed rows, surface reason codes when not deduped.
- console: show provisional badge and reason code with link to raw ledger rows.;
oliver: edge-case: what if reconnect legitimately routes to different region for latency and we want to charge both? rule: if route_tag changes AND prefix matched, treat as continuation; if route_tag changes AND prefix doesn't match, treat as new session. how detect prefix match reliably? KV cache prefix length compare?;
kevin: compare `kv_prefix_checksum` or `prefix_length` in ledger rows. if prefix_length >= threshold (e.g., 128 tokens) then continuation.;
jess: careful with privacy — checksum ok, avoid raw text.;
mariam: i'll draft the ledger schema change PR and a short console UX mockup. timeline: schema PR today, runtime attempt to reuse billing_session_id as experiment in canary.;
deploy-bot: canary deploy of billing-session-id-propagation succeeded in eu-west-1-a (version=canary-2026-03-21).;
kevin: for billing reconciliation, ops: run a one-off query to find invoices where sum(provisional+confirmed) > confirmed and surface top 20 customers. i'll own that. :eyes:;
jess: add an alert when provisional rows older than 24h without a confirm or supersede. that would have flagged this earlier.;
mariam: opening tickets: ENG-PLATFORM-1421 (ledger schema), ENG-RUNTIME-876 (billing_session reuse), ENG-CONSOLE-501 (UX flags). will ping infra for backfill guidance.;
oliver: quick question: any risk to token accounting accuracy if we coalesce provisional -> confirmed? must ensure we don't underbill on real multi-route retries.;
kevin: if we coalesce only when billing_session_id and prefix match rules hold we should be safe. include audit log entries for all supersedes so we can reverse if needed.;
mariam: ok creating PRs and will post links once available. thanks all :+1:
